    <bpmn:process id="W_W828" name="W828. Ecommerce Platform Feature Release, A/B Testing &amp; UX Optimization" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Feature development completed per W132 software development; UX improvement identified per analytics
Frequency: Bi-weekly release cycles; ~2–4 A/B tests running concurrently
Volume: ~24 releases/year; ~50–100 A/B tests/year; ~300–500 UX improvements/year
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager
Participants: Product Manager, UX Designer, Developer, QA Tester, Marketing Manager, Business Analyst
Source: workflow W828 — Ecommerce Platform Feature Release, A/B Testing &amp; UX Optimization</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W828_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W828_Lane1" name="Product Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W828_Lane2" name="UX Designer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W828_Lane3" name="Developer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W828_End14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W828_Start5" name="Feature development completed per W132 software development; UX improvement identified…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task6" name="Feature release plan creation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Feature release plan creation: Product Manager creates feature release plan: (a) feature description and user stories; (b) success metrics (conversion rate, bounce rate, AOV, cart abandonment); (c) target audience segment per W156 CDP; (d) release strategy (A/B test vs. gradual rollout vs. full release)
Responsible (R): Product Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 2-4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task7" name="A/B test feature setup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: A/B test feature setup: for A/B test features: (a) UX Designer creates variant(s) per hypothesis; (b) Developer implements feature flags per W132; (c) QA Tester validates both control and variant experiences per W391; (d) configure traffic split (typically 50/50 or 80/20 for high-risk changes)
Responsible (R): UX Designer / Developer / QA Tester
Accountable (A): Product Manager
Duration: 4-8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task8" name="Release deployment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Release deployment: (a) deploy to staging environment per W384; (b) QA regression test per W391; (c) deploy to production with feature flag off; (d) enable for test group; (e) monitor W725 platform health dashboard for 24 hours
Responsible (R): Developer / QA Tester
Accountable (A): Product Manager
Duration: 4-8 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task9" name="A/B test monitoring (1-4 weeks)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: A/B test monitoring (1-4 weeks): (a) daily metric comparison (control vs. variant); (b) statistical significance tracking; (c) segment analysis (mobile vs. desktop, new vs. returning, by region); (d) watch for negative impacts on W557 cart abandonment or W98 cancellation rates
Responsible (R): Product Manager / Business Analyst
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 30 min/day × test duration</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task10" name="A/B test conclusion">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: A/B test conclusion: (a) if variant wins: full rollout to 100% traffic; (b) if no significant difference: revert to control, document learnings; (c) if variant loses: revert immediately, analyze why
Responsible (R): Product Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 2-3 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task11" name="Non-A/B gradual rollout">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Non-A/B gradual rollout: for non-A/B releases: (a) gradual rollout — 10% → 25% → 50% → 100% over 1-2 weeks; (b) monitoring at each stage; (c) instant rollback capability per W659 incident management
Responsible (R): Developer / Product Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 1-2 hours per stage</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task12" name="Post-release documentation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Post-release documentation: (a) Product Manager documents results in feature log; (b) Business Analyst updates conversion funnel analytics per W113 BI; (c) Marketing Manager notified for promotional integration per W83
Responsible (R): Product Manager / Business Analyst
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 1-2 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W828_Task13" name="Monthly UX optimization review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Monthly UX optimization review: (a) conversion funnel analysis; (b) top exit pages; (c) mobile vs. desktop performance; (d) page load time per W725 monitoring; (e) customer feedback per W510 reviews and W41 complaints
Responsible (R): Product Manager / UX Designer
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Ops Mgr
Duration: 4-6 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W828_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W828_End14" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W828_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W828_Annotation15">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: periodic feature-flag cleanup
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
