    <bpmn:process id="W_W1034" name="W1034. Customer Ecommerce Payment Failure Recovery, Retry &amp; Abandoned Checkout Rescue" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Ecommerce payment transaction fails; or customer abandons checkout before payment completion
Frequency: ~8,000–12,000 payment failures/month (~18–25% of ecommerce checkout attempts); ~15,000–20,000 abandoned checkouts/month
Volume: 1 event per failed payment or abandoned checkout
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Customer, Payment Gateway Provider, Customer Service Agent (for manual recovery)
Source: workflow W1034 — Customer Ecommerce Payment Failure Recovery, Retry &amp; Abandoned Checkout Rescue</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1034_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1034_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1034_Lane2" name="Ecommerce Operations Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1034_End10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1034_Start4" name="Ecommerce payment transaction fails; or customer abandons checkout before payment…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1034_Task5" name="Payment Failure Detection &amp; Classification">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Payment Failure Detection &amp; Classification: When a payment transaction fails at checkout: (a) system captures: payment method attempted, error code from payment gateway (PayMongo/Dragonpay), error category (card declined, insufficient funds, timeout, authentication failure, network error, fraud suspicion, bank timeout); (b) system classifies failure into recovery strategy: Retryable (timeout, network error, bank temporary decline — customer can retry immediately), Alternative Method (card declined — suggest GCash/Maya/bank transfer instead), Customer Action Required (authentication failure, insufficient funds — customer must resolve with bank), Fraud Block (legitimate fraud suspicion — no retry, route to fraud review per W266); (c) system displays contextual error message to customer with suggested next action: &quot;Your card payment was declined. Would you like to pay with GCash instead?&quot; or &quot;Payment timed out. Please try again.&quot;
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: &lt; 5 sec (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1034_Task6" name="Automated Retry &amp; Payment Method Switching">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated Retry &amp; Payment Method Switching: For retryable failures: (a) system offers one-click retry with same payment method (customer taps &quot;Try Again&quot;); (b) if retry also fails, system automatically displays alternative payment methods with the same order: &quot;Your card payment failed twice. Try GCash — it&#x27;s fast and easy!&quot;; (c) system saves the complete order (items, delivery address, delivery slot) for 72 hours — customer can return and complete payment without re-shopping; (d) for bank transfer payments: system generates unique reference number and provides step-by-step instructions with bank links; customer has 24 hours to complete transfer before order expires; (e) system tracks conversion rate per failure-to-recovery path for optimization
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: &lt; 30 sec (automated)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1034_Task7" name="Abandoned Checkout Recovery Sequence">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Abandoned Checkout Recovery Sequence: For customers who abandon checkout (leave the page without completing payment): (a) Immediate (0–30 min): system sends browser push notification (if permission granted): &quot;You left items in your cart. Complete your purchase now!&quot; with deep link to checkout page; (b) 1 hour: email triggered with cart summary, item images, and &quot;Complete Your Order&quot; button — email links to pre-populated checkout page (items, address, delivery slot preserved); (c) 24 hours: follow-up email with social proof: &quot;This item is selling fast — only X left in stock at your nearest store&quot; (real inventory data); include urgency trigger; (d) 48 hours: final recovery email with incentive (if margin allows): &quot;Complete your order within 24 hours and get PHP 100 off with code COMEBACK100&quot; — discount code auto-generated and single-use; (e) 72 hours: abandoned order released; inventory returned to available stock; delivery slot released; (f) system tracks recovery rate at each touchpoint for funnel optimization per W565
Responsible (R): System / Email Engine
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1034_Task8" name="Payment Gateway Health Monitoring &amp; Failover">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Payment Gateway Health Monitoring &amp; Failover: Ecommerce Operations team monitors payment gateway health: (a) real-time dashboard: payment success rate by method, average processing time, error rate by type, gateway uptime; (b) if a specific payment method&#x27;s success rate drops below 85% for 30+ minutes: (i) system sends alert to Ecommerce Operations Manager, (ii) investigate: is this a gateway issue (PayMongo outage), bank-wide issue (BDO offline), or BuildRight configuration issue? (iii) if gateway issue: contact PayMongo/Dragonpay support for ETA; (iv) temporarily de-emphasize affected payment method at checkout (reduce visual prominence, add &quot;experiencing delays&quot; notice); (v) redirect customers to alternative payment methods; (c) maintain at least 3 active payment gateways to prevent single-point-of-failure; (d) monthly payment gateway performance review with providers per W99 (Payment Settlement Reconciliation)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Operations Manager / IT
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 15–30 min/day (monitoring)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1034_Task9" name="Recovery Analytics &amp; Continuous Optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Recovery Analytics &amp; Continuous Optimization: Monthly: (a) analyze payment failure funnel: checkout attempts → payment attempts → successful payments, with drop-off at each stage; (b) calculate recovery rate: % of failed payments eventually converted through retry, method switch, or recovery sequence; (c) analyze failure patterns: (i) which payment methods have highest failure rates? (ii) which banks/issuers decline most frequently? (iii) is there a time-of-day pattern (peak GCash timeout during lunch hour)? (d) optimize: (i) adjust checkout flow to pre-qualify payment methods (detect likely declines before submission), (ii) add new payment methods (e.g., ShopeePay, GrabPay — popular Philippine e-wallets), (iii) negotiate better gateway routing with PayMongo to reduce timeout rates; (e) benchmark: BuildRight&#x27;s payment success rate vs. Philippine ecommerce industry average (~75–80%)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Operations Manager / IT
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 2–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1034_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1034_End10" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1034_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1034_Annotation11">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: Ecommerce Operations Manager review and approval gate; operational: periodic reconciliation against source documents
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
