    <bpmn:process id="W_W1287" name="W1287. Customer Ecommerce Product Availability Notification &amp; Back-in-Stock Alert" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer requests notification when an out-of-stock product becomes available
Frequency: ~3,000–5,000 back-in-stock alert subscriptions per month
Volume: ~15–25% of out-of-stock product page visits result in alert subscription
Owner: Ecommerce Operations
Participants: Ecommerce Operations, Customer, Supply Planning, Category Manager
Source: workflow W1287 — Customer Ecommerce Product Availability Notification &amp; Back-in-Stock Alert</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1287_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1287_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1287_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1287_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1287_Start4" name="Customer requests notification when an out-of-stock product becomes available">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task5" name="Alert subscription">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Alert subscription: Customer visits out-of-stock product page on ecommerce; system displays &quot;Notify me when available&quot; button with channel options (email, SMS, app push); customer clicks to subscribe; system records: (a) customer ID (loyalty member or guest), (b) product SKU, (c) preferred notification channel, (d) timestamp, (e) customer&#x27;s nearest store (for BOPIS availability)
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task6" name="Demand signal aggregation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Demand signal aggregation: System aggregates back-in-stock subscriptions: (a) total subscriptions per SKU, (b) subscriptions per SKU per store region, (c) subscription velocity (how fast subscriptions accumulate — indicates demand urgency); feeds aggregated demand signal to Supply Planning: (a) if subscriptions &gt; threshold (e.g., 50 for A-items, 20 for B-items): triggers expedited replenishment review per W2A, (b) if subscriptions concentrated in specific region: prioritizes regional DC replenishment
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task7" name="Inventory replenishment event">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Inventory replenishment event: When out-of-stock SKU is replenished (goods receipt posted at DC or store per W3 or W109): (a) system detects inventory change for subscribed SKU, (b) checks if inventory level exceeds subscription count + safety stock (enough to fulfill alerts), (c) if sufficient stock: triggers notification batch; if insufficient: queues notification until sufficient stock available
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task8" name="Customer notification dispatch">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Customer notification dispatch: System sends back-in-stock alert to subscribed customers: (a) email with product image, &quot;Back in Stock&quot; badge, and direct &quot;Add to Cart&quot; link, (b) SMS with product name and direct link, (c) app push notification; notifications sent in subscription order (first subscribed, first notified); batch size limited to available inventory to avoid overselling
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task9" name="Conversion tracking">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Conversion tracking: System tracks back-in-stock alert conversion funnel: (a) notifications sent, (b) email/SMS open rate, (c) click-through to product page, (d) add-to-cart rate, (e) purchase completion rate, (f) average time from notification to purchase; weekly conversion report to Ecommerce Operations and Category Manager
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1287_Task10" name="Alert expiry &amp; cleanup">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Alert expiry &amp; cleanup: System manages alert lifecycle: (a) alerts expire after 90 days if item not restocked (per the W930 canonical expiry, with T-60 reconfirmation), (b) customer receives &quot;we&#x27;re sorry this item is still unavailable&quot; message with alternative product suggestions, (c) subscription removed from active queue, (d) for items not restocked within 60 days: Category Manager reviews for seasonal discontinuation per W264 or vendor supply issue escalation per W36
Responsible (R): System / Category Manager
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations
Duration: Automated + 30 min/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1287_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1287_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1287_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1287_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: limiting notification batch to available quantity and first-come-first-served
Owner: Ecommerce Operations</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1287_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1287_Annotation12" targetRef="W1287_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow14" sourceRef="W1287_Start4" targetRef="W1287_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow15" sourceRef="W1287_Task5" targetRef="W1287_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow16" sourceRef="W1287_Task6" targetRef="W1287_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow17" sourceRef="W1287_Task7" targetRef="W1287_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow18" sourceRef="W1287_Task8" targetRef="W1287_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow19" sourceRef="W1287_Task9" targetRef="W1287_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1287_Flow20" sourceRef="W1287_Task10" targetRef="W1287_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1287_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1287_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1287">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1287_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1287_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1580" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
