    <bpmn:process id="W_W1360" name="W1360. Omnichannel Inventory Reservation, Oversell Prevention &amp; Multi-Channel Stock Allocation Governance" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer places ecommerce order (BOPIS or home delivery); or store replenishment order is released; or large B2B project order is confirmed
Frequency: Continuous; ~42,900 ecommerce orders/month + ~50,000 store replenishment orders/month (production-calibrated per data-volumes §1.1) + ~3,500 AR invoices/month competing for the same inventory pool
Volume: 35,000 active SKUs across 205 locations (200 stores + 4 DCs + 1 HQ); at any moment, ~5–10% of SKUs (1,750–3,500) are in constrained supply status
Owner: Supply Planning Manager
Participants: Supply Planning Manager, Ecommerce Manager, Category Manager, DC Operations Manager, B2B Sales Manager
Source: workflow W1360 — Omnichannel Inventory Reservation, Oversell Prevention &amp; Multi-Channel Stock Allocation Governance</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1360_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1360_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1360_Lane2" name="Supply Planning Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1360_Lane3" name="Ecommerce Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1360_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1360_Start5" name="Customer places ecommerce order (BOPIS or home delivery); or store replenishment order is…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1360_Task6" name="System maintains real-time available-to-promise (ATP) quantity per SKU per…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: System maintains real-time available-to-promise (ATP) quantity per SKU per location: on-hand − reserved (open orders) − allocated (replenishment) − safety stock = available for new orders
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Real-time</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1360_Task7" name="Ecommerce customer places order: system checks ATP at fulfillment location…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Ecommerce customer places order: system checks ATP at fulfillment location (store for BOPIS, DC for home delivery); if ATP &gt; 0, reserves quantity and confirms order; if ATP = 0, shows &quot;Out of Stock&quot; on product page
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1360_Task8" name="BOPIS reservation timeout: if customer does not pick up within 5 days, system…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: BOPIS reservation timeout: if customer does not pick up within 5 days, system auto-cancels order and releases reserved inventory back to ATP pool
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1360_Task9" name="For constrained SKUs (ATP &lt; 2× average daily demand across channels): Supply…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: For constrained SKUs (ATP &lt; 2× average daily demand across channels): Supply Planning Manager reviews allocation priorities weekly using configurable allocation rules engine (e.g., 50% store replenishment, 30% ecommerce, 20% B2B project — percentages adjustable per SKU category)
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 2–3 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1360_Task10" name="Large B2B project order (&gt; PHP 500K or &gt; 20% of a single SKU&#x27;s on-hand at any…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Large B2B project order (&gt; PHP 500K or &gt; 20% of a single SKU&#x27;s on-hand at any location): requires Supply Planning Manager approval before reservation is confirmed; Manager evaluates impact on store replenishment and ecommerce availability
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 15–30 min/order</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1360_Task11" name="Ecommerce oversell incident (system confirms order but inventory not physically…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Ecommerce oversell incident (system confirms order but inventory not physically available at fulfillment location): triggers immediate customer notification, order cancellation or alternative fulfillment location offer, and ATP recalculation audit
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Manager / System
Accountable (A): Supply Planning Manager
Duration: 15 min/incident</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1360_Task12" name="Monthly allocation effectiveness review: Supply Planning Manager analyzes…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly allocation effectiveness review: Supply Planning Manager analyzes stockout frequency by channel, allocation rule utilization, and oversell incident rate; adjusts allocation parameters
Responsible (R): Supply Planning Manager
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1360_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1360_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1360_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1360_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: Supply Planning Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Supply Planning Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1360_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1360_Annotation14" targetRef="W1360_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
