    <bpmn:process id="W_W1502" name="W1502. Customer E-Commerce Product Comparison Tool, Alternate/Substitute Product Recommendation &amp; Cross-Sell Engine" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer browses a product page on the BuildRight ecommerce platform or mobile app
Frequency: Continuous — every product page view triggers comparison and recommendation logic
Volume: ~500,000–1,000,000 product page views/month; ~3–5 comparison/recommendation widgets per page
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager
Participants: Ecommerce Product Manager, Merchandise Analyst, UI/UX Designer, Data Engineer
Source: workflow W1502 — Customer E-Commerce Product Comparison Tool, Alternate/Substitute Product Recommendation &amp; Cross-Sell Engine</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1502_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1502_Lane1" name="Merchandise Analyst">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1502_Lane2" name="Ecommerce Product Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1502_Lane3" name="Data Engineer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1502_End11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1502_Start5" name="Customer browses a product page on the BuildRight ecommerce platform or mobile app">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1502_Task6" name="Product attribute enrichment">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Product attribute enrichment: (a) Merchandise Analyst ensures every product in the ecommerce catalog has: (i) standardized attribute taxonomy: category, subcategory, material, dimensions, weight, color, brand, application, coverage area, drying time (for paint/adhesives), load capacity (for hardware); (ii) comparable attributes: all products in the same subcategory must have the same set of attributes filled; (iii) normalized values: &quot;1 gallon&quot; vs. &quot;3.78L&quot; vs. &quot;4L&quot; normalized to standard unit; (b) attribute completeness score calculated per SKU — only SKUs with &gt; 80% attribute completeness participate in comparison and recommendation features
Responsible (R): Merchandise Analyst
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Product Manager
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1502_Task7" name="Comparison widget configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Comparison widget configuration: (a) Ecommerce Product Manager configures comparison rules per product category: (i) which attributes are displayed in the comparison table (e.g., for tiles: material, size, thickness, finish, price per sqm, slip rating); (ii) which attributes are highlighted as &quot;key differentiators&quot; (bold/highlighted in UI); (iii) maximum number of products in a single comparison (typically 3–4); (b) comparison data pulled from PIM (Product Information Management) system in real-time; (c) comparison widget renders on the product page and in a dedicated comparison view
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Product Manager / Data Engineer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Per category setup: 2–4 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1502_Task8" name="Substitute product recommendation engine">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Substitute product recommendation engine: (a) rules-based + ML-powered recommendation engine generates substitute suggestions: (i) rules-based: same subcategory, same or adjacent price range, same key attributes (e.g., &quot;also available in 5-gallon size&quot;); (ii) ML-powered: &quot;customers who viewed this product also viewed&quot; based on browsing history; (iii) collaborative filtering: &quot;customers who bought this product also bought&quot; based on purchase history; (b) recommendations displayed as: &quot;Similar Products&quot; carousel on product page; (c) Merchandise Analyst reviews recommendation accuracy monthly: (i) click-through rate (target: &gt; 8%); (ii) add-to-cart rate from recommendations (target: &gt; 3%); (iii) recommendation relevance score from periodic manual audit
Responsible (R): Data Engineer / Ecommerce Product Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: Ongoing with monthly review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1502_Task9" name="Cross-sell &amp; project bundle suggestions">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-sell &amp; project bundle suggestions: (a) system generates cross-sell recommendations: (i) &quot;Frequently Bought Together&quot; — items with &gt; 15% co-purchase rate; (ii) &quot;Complete Your Project&quot; — project-based bundles (e.g., tile + adhesive + grout + spacers + trowel); (iii) &quot;Required Accessories&quot; — mandatory companion items (e.g., paint thinner for oil-based paint); (b) cross-sell displayed at three points in the purchase journey: (i) product page (&quot;Frequently Bought Together&quot;); (ii) cart page (&quot;Don&#x27;t forget these essentials&quot;); (iii) checkout page (&quot;Last chance to add&quot;); (d) bundle pricing: cross-sell items offered at 5–10% bundle discount when added together
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Product Manager / Merchandise Analyst
Accountable (A): VP Merchandising
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1502_Task10" name="Recommendation engine performance monitoring">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Recommendation engine performance monitoring: Monthly: (a) Ecommerce Product Manager reviews KPIs: (i) recommendation click-through rate by widget type; (ii) add-to-cart rate from recommendations; (iii) average order value with vs. without recommendation interaction; (iv) revenue attributed to recommendations; (b) A/B testing: (i) test new recommendation algorithms against baseline; (ii) test different widget placements and designs; (iii) test bundle discount levels (5% vs. 10% vs. 15%); (c) underperforming recommendation categories investigated and reconfigured; (d) Data Engineer retrains ML models quarterly with fresh purchase/browsing data
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Product Manager / Data Engineer
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 1 day/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1502_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1502_End11" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1502_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1502_Annotation12">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: Ecommerce Product Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1502_Assoc13" sourceRef="W1502_Annotation12" targetRef="W1502_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow14" sourceRef="W1502_Start5" targetRef="W1502_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow15" sourceRef="W1502_Task6" targetRef="W1502_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow16" sourceRef="W1502_Task7" targetRef="W1502_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow17" sourceRef="W1502_Task8" targetRef="W1502_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow18" sourceRef="W1502_Task9" targetRef="W1502_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1502_Flow19" sourceRef="W1502_Task10" targetRef="W1502_End11" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1502_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1502_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1502">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1370" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Task6_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Task6"><dc:Bounds x="400" y="125" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Task7_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Task7"><dc:Bounds x="610" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Task8_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Task8"><dc:Bounds x="820" y="465" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Task9_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Task9"><dc:Bounds x="1030" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Task10_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Task10"><dc:Bounds x="1240" y="295" width="180" height="80" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Start5_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Start5"><dc:Bounds x="290" y="147" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_End11_di" bpmnElement="W1502_End11"><dc:Bounds x="1470" y="487" width="36" height="36" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1502_Annotation12_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Annotation12"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="630" width="360" height="60" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow14_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow14"><di:waypoint x="326" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="400" y="165" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow15_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow15"><di:waypoint x="580" y="165" /><di:waypoint x="610" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow16_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow16"><di:waypoint x="790" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="820" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow17_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow17"><di:waypoint x="1000" y="505" /><di:waypoint x="1030" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow18_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow18"><di:waypoint x="1210" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1240" y="335" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Flow19_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Flow19"><di:waypoint x="1420" y="335" /><di:waypoint x="1470" y="505" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
        <bpmndi:BPMNEdge id="W1502_Assoc13_di" bpmnElement="W1502_Assoc13"><di:waypoint x="340" y="630" /><di:waypoint x="308" y="183" /></bpmndi:BPMNEdge>
      </bpmndi:BPMNPlane>
    </bpmndi:BPMNDiagram>
    <bpmn:process id="W_W1510" name="W1510. Customer Digital Home Project Planner, Materials Calculator &amp; Shopping List" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer accesses &quot;Project Planner&quot; on buildright.com.ph or mobile app; or scans QR code on in-store project display (e.g., kitchen display, bathroom vignette)
Frequency: ~10,000–15,000 project planner sessions/month
Volume: ~30% of sessions result in a saved shopping list; ~10–15% convert to an order within 30 days
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager
Participants: Customer, Ecommerce Product Manager, Category Manager (content), Digital Content Team
Source: workflow W1510 — Customer Digital Home Project Planner, Materials Calculator &amp; Shopping List</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1510_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1510_Lane1" name="Customer">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1510_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1510_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1510_Start4" name="Customer accesses &quot;Project Planner&quot; on buildright.com.ph or mobile app; or scans QR code…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1510_Task5" name="Project type selection">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Project type selection: Customer selects project type from template library: (a) bathroom renovation, (b) kitchen renovation, (c) room painting, (d) tile flooring, (e) electrical wiring, (f) plumbing installation, (g) fence/gate construction, (h) custom (free-form); each template pre-loads relevant product categories and calculation formulas
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1510_Task6" name="Room dimensions input">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Room dimensions input: Customer enters room/area dimensions: (a) length, width, and height of the room, (b) number and dimensions of doors and windows (for paint/tile deduction), (c) for tile projects: select tile size from available inventory, (d) for painting projects: number of coats, surface type (concrete, wood, metal); system validates inputs and provides real-time area calculations
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 3–5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1510_Task7" name="Materials calculation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Materials calculation: System auto-calculates material requirements based on project template and dimensions: (a) tiles: total floor area ÷ tile area × 1.10 (10% waste factor for cuts and breakage), matched to available tile SKUs with real-time inventory and pricing, (b) adhesive: kg per sqm based on tile size, (c) grout: linear meters of grout lines × grout width, (d) paint: area × coverage rate per liter × number of coats, (e) plumbing fittings: standard fitting list based on fixture count (1 toilet = wax ring, supply line, angle valve, etc.), (f) electrical: wire length estimate based on room perimeter × outlet/switch count; system shows calculated quantities with unit prices and subtotals
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1510_Task8" name="Product selection &amp; customization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Product selection &amp; customization: Customer reviews auto-generated materials list and customizes: (a) swap calculated tile SKU for a different design (system recalculates price, checks inventory), (b) select paint color from swatch (system links to tinting options per W168), (c) add optional items not in template (e.g., accessories, tools, PPE), (d) remove items already owned, (e) adjust quantities if desired
Responsible (R): Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–15 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1510_Task9" name="Budget check &amp; optimization">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Budget check &amp; optimization: System provides budget tools: (a) total project cost with breakdown by category (materials, delivery, optional installation service per W138), (b) &quot;Value Option&quot; alternatives: suggest lower-cost items for budget-conscious customers (e.g., local brand tiles vs. imported), (c) financing estimate: if project &gt; PHP 50,000, display monthly installment amount per W1508 financing options, (d) trade pricing: if customer is a trade account holder per W1507, auto-apply trade discount
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1510_Task10" name="Save &amp; share">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Save &amp; share: Customer saves project plan: (a) saved to customer account (or as guest with email link), (b) shareable link for contractor/spouse review, (c) printable PDF with materials list, quantities, and product images, (d) option to generate an in-store quotation: customer can visit store and Sales Associate can recall the project plan from customer&#x27;s account for face-to-face consultation
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 1 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1510_Task11" name="Convert to order">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Convert to order: Customer proceeds to checkout: (a) shopping list auto-populates cart with calculated quantities, (b) system checks inventory availability at preferred store or DC, (c) customer selects fulfillment: (i) BOPIS at preferred store, (ii) home delivery per ECOM-011, (iii) bulk jobsite delivery per W1509 if applicable, (d) customer completes payment; or (e) customer clicks &quot;Visit Store&quot; — system sends shopping list to customer&#x27;s preferred store for Sales Associate preparation
Responsible (R): Customer / System
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Product Mgr
Duration: 5 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1510_Task12" name="Abandoned plan retargeting">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Abandoned plan retargeting: For saved project plans not converted within 7 days: (a) system sends reminder email with project summary, (b) Day 14: send promotional email with &quot;Complete Your Project&quot; incentive (e.g., free delivery, 5% discount on project items), (c) track abandonment reasons through analytics: price sensitivity, scope uncertainty, seasonal timing
Responsible (R): System / Ecommerce Product Mgr
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1510_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1510_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1510_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1510_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: generous waste factors (10–15%) and clear disclaimer that estimates are guidelines, not guarantees; operational: positioning the planner as a customer tool for homeowners, with the saved list shareable to their contractor
Owner: Ecommerce Product Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
