    <bpmn:process id="W_W1512" name="W1512. Omnichannel Customer Unified Profile, Identity Resolution &amp; Cross-Channel Activity Merge" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: New customer interaction across any channel (POS, ecommerce, call center, loyalty program, trade account) where identity cannot be automatically matched to existing profile; or scheduled weekly batch identity resolution run
Frequency: Continuous real-time matching + weekly batch reconciliation
Volume: ~600,000 loyalty members + ~5,400 trade/corporate accounts + ~2.8M monthly POS transactions (many from unregistered walk-in customers) + ~42,900 monthly ecommerce orders; estimated ~50,000–100,000 identity resolution actions/month
Owner: CRM / Data Manager
Participants: CRM Data Steward, IT Data Engineering, Marketing Analyst, Customer Service Manager
Source: workflow W1512 — Omnichannel Customer Unified Profile, Identity Resolution &amp; Cross-Channel Activity Merge</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1512_LaneSet4">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1512_Lane1" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Start5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1512_Lane2" name="CRM Data Steward">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1512_Lane3" name="CRM Data Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1512_End13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1512_Start5" name="New customer interaction across any channel (POS, ecommerce, call center, loyalty…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1512_Task6" name="Real-time identity matching at point of interaction">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Real-time identity matching at point of interaction: At every customer interaction, system attempts real-time matching: (a) POS: customer presents loyalty card/QR — system matches to loyalty profile by card number; customer provides mobile number — system searches by mobile; if no match: create anonymous transaction linked to POS terminal/store/date, (b) ecommerce: customer logs in — system matches by authenticated email/phone; guest checkout — system matches by email address + mobile number against existing profiles; if no match: create new profile, (c) call center: customer provides name or mobile — agent searches CRM; if multiple matches found: verify with additional identifiers (address, last purchase details), (d) trade account: customer presents trade QR per W1507 — system matches by trade account number; cross-reference with loyalty profile if customer also has a loyalty account
Responsible (R): System / Cashier / Agent
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: Automated (real-time)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1512_Task7" name="Automated identity resolution (batch)">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Automated identity resolution (batch): Weekly, data engineering runs batch identity resolution: (a) deterministic matching: exact match on government-issued ID number (TIN, driver&#x27;s license), mobile number, or email address across all channels — these are high-confidence matches merged automatically, (b) probabilistic matching: fuzzy match on name + address + mobile prefix + purchase pattern similarity — these generate &quot;potential match&quot; records requiring manual review, (c) household matching: link family members sharing the same address or payment method (e.g., husband&#x27;s trade account + wife&#x27;s loyalty account) — household-level aggregation for marketing but individual-level for privacy compliance, (d) match confidence scoring: (i) High (&gt;95%): auto-merge profiles, (ii) Medium (70–95%): queue for Data Steward review, (iii) Low (&lt;70%): no action, maintain separate profiles
Responsible (R): System / Data Engineering
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: 4–6 hours/week (batch run + review)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1512_Task8" name="Manual identity review &amp; merge">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Manual identity review &amp; merge: CRM Data Steward reviews medium-confidence matches: (a) review side-by-side profile comparison: name, mobile, email, address, purchase history, loyalty activity, trade account details, (b) verify using additional evidence: (i) same payment method used across channels, (ii) delivery address matches billing address, (iii) customer self-identified across channels (e.g., loyalty member mentioned trade account during call center interaction), (c) decision: merge profiles (creating unified profile with all channel history) or reject match (maintain separate profiles), (d) merged profile retains all channel activity history; primary identifier selected based on most-recently-used channel
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: 10–15 min per review</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1512_Task9" name="Cross-channel conflict resolution">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Cross-channel conflict resolution: When merging profiles reveals conflicting data: (a) name variation: &quot;Juan Dela Cruz&quot; vs. &quot;Juan D. Cruz&quot; — prefer verified ID name (from trade account or loyalty registration), (b) contact information: multiple mobile numbers or email addresses — retain all as active; designate primary per customer preference or most-recently-used, (c) address: multiple addresses — designate one as primary (most recent delivery or billing address); retain others as secondary, (d) pricing tier: if customer has both loyalty (retail pricing) and trade account (trade pricing) — designate trade pricing as default when trade QR is scanned; retail pricing when loyalty card is scanned; system supports dual-tier pricing per customer, (e) loyalty points: consolidate points from duplicate accounts into unified profile; adjust tier calculation based on total cross-channel spend
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward / System
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: 5–10 min per conflict</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1512_Task10" name="Data privacy compliance integration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Data privacy compliance integration: Unified profile supports RA 10173 compliance: (a) data subject access request: customer requests all data BuildRight holds — system generates unified report from all channel profiles (POS transactions, ecommerce orders, loyalty activity, call recordings, service orders), (b) consent management: customer&#x27;s marketing consent preferences are applied uniformly across all channels (if customer opts out of SMS marketing, suppress SMS across POS, ecommerce, and call center), (c) data deletion request: upon verified request, system anonymizes customer profile across all channels while retaining transactional data required by BIR (10-year retention per NFR-006) — replace PII with anonymized identifier, (d) data breach notification: if unified profile is compromised, notify customer once with full scope of affected data across all channels per NFR-016
Responsible (R): CRM Data Steward / Legal (DPO)
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: 30–60 min per request</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1512_Task11" name="Unified profile activation">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Unified profile activation: Merged profiles power cross-channel capabilities: (a) POS: cashier sees customer&#x27;s online browsing history and abandoned cart items — can suggest products or offer in-store pickup of online items, (b) ecommerce: customer sees in-store purchase history and loyalty point balance — can redeem points online, (c) call center: agent sees complete interaction history across all channels — resolves inquiries faster, (d) marketing: segmented campaigns based on total customer value (not just single-channel activity), (e) trade customers: personalized trade pricing auto-applied at POS and ecommerce when identified, (f) installation services: customer&#x27;s service history and warranty registrations visible across all channels
Responsible (R): System / All customer-facing roles
Accountable (A): CRM Data Mgr
Duration: Ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1512_Task12" name="Monthly identity resolution analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Monthly identity resolution analytics: CRM Data Manager reviews: (a) match rate: % of transactions successfully linked to a known profile, (b) duplicate rate: estimated number of duplicate profiles in the database, (c) merge accuracy: % of merged profiles verified as correct (sampling), (d) channel linkage: % of customers active on 2+ channels (target: 25% within Year 1), (e) profile completeness: % of profiles with name + mobile + email + address, (f) data quality score: overall database health metric
Responsible (R): CRM Data Manager
Accountable (A): VP Marketing
Duration: 3–4 hours/month</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1512_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1512_End13" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1512_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1512_Annotation14">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: requiring additional identifiers (mobile number, address) for medium-confidence matches and manual review; operational: POS prompts encouraging mobile number entry and ecommerce email validation; operational: phased approach — start with high-value trade accounts, then loyalty members, then anonymous-to-known matching
Owner: CRM / Data Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1512_Assoc15" sourceRef="W1512_Annotation14" targetRef="W1512_Start5" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow16" sourceRef="W1512_Start5" targetRef="W1512_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow17" sourceRef="W1512_Task6" targetRef="W1512_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow18" sourceRef="W1512_Task7" targetRef="W1512_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow19" sourceRef="W1512_Task8" targetRef="W1512_Task9" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow20" sourceRef="W1512_Task9" targetRef="W1512_Task10" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow21" sourceRef="W1512_Task10" targetRef="W1512_Task11" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow22" sourceRef="W1512_Task11" targetRef="W1512_Task12" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1512_Flow23" sourceRef="W1512_Task12" targetRef="W1512_End13" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W1512_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W1512_plane" bpmnElement="W_W1512">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1512_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W1512_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1512_Lane2_di" bpmnElement="W1512_Lane2" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="250" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W1512_Lane3_di" bpmnElement="W1512_Lane3" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="420" width="1790" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
