    <bpmn:process id="W_W1548" name="W1548. Ecommerce Customer Product Bundle Builder &amp; Custom Project Kit Assembly Order Processing" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Customer initiates a &quot;Build Your Own Bundle&quot; or &quot;Project Kit&quot; on the ecommerce platform
Frequency: ~200–300 bundle orders/month (new feature, growing)
Volume: Average 3–5 items per custom bundle; higher AOV than individual item orders
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: Customer, Ecommerce Platform, Merchandising Team, DC Pick/Pack Team
Source: workflow W1548 — Ecommerce Customer Product Bundle Builder &amp; Custom Project Kit Assembly Order Processing</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W1548_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W1548_Lane1" name="Merchandising Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1548_Lane2" name="System">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1548_Lane3" name="DC Pick">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W1548_Lane4" name="Ecommerce Ops Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W1548_End12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W1548_Start6" name="Customer initiates a &quot;Build Your Own Bundle&quot; or &quot;Project Kit&quot; on the ecommerce platform">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow15</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1548_Task7" name="Bundle template configuration">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Bundle template configuration: Merchandising Team creates bundle templates per project type — e.g., &quot;Bathroom Renovation Kit&quot; includes tile category (select 1), adhesive (select 1), grout (select 1), waterproofing (optional), tools (optional); defines compatibility rules (certain tiles require specific adhesive types), minimum/maximum item counts, and bundle discount percentage (typically 5–10% vs. individual purchase)
Responsible (R): Merchandising Team
Accountable (A): Category Manager
Duration: 2–3 hours/template</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow15</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow16</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1548_Task8" name="Customer bundle building">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Customer bundle building: Customer selects project type on ecommerce platform; system presents compatible product options filtered by availability (real-time ATP from W533); customer selects items; system validates compatibility rules and applies bundle discount; dynamic price updates with each selection
Responsible (R): System / Customer
Accountable (A): —
Duration: 5–10 min</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow16</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow17</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:serviceTask id="W1548_Task9" name="Order processing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Order processing: Customer places bundle order; system creates single order with line items flagged as &quot;Bundle: [Template Name]&quot;; applies bundle discount as line-level price adjustment; calculates single delivery fee (not per-item); loyalty points calculated on discounted total
Responsible (R): System
Accountable (A): —
Duration: Automated</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow17</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:serviceTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1548_Task10" name="DC pick &amp; pack">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: DC pick &amp; pack: Bundle order flows to assigned DC (W536); picker receives consolidated pick list with bundle identifier; packs all bundle items together in a single shipment package when possible; applies &quot;Your Project Kit&quot; branded packaging insert
Responsible (R): DC Pick/Pack Team
Accountable (A): DC Supervisor
Duration: 10–15 min/bundle</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W1548_Task11" name="Bundle analytics">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Bundle analytics: Ecommerce Operations Manager reviews bundle performance weekly — conversion rate (browse to purchase), average items per bundle, most/least popular items by template, AOV comparison (bundle vs. individual), fulfillment accuracy for multi-item bundles
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Manager
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 2 hours/week</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W1548_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W1548_End12" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W1548_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W1548_Annotation13">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).) | - operational: Ecommerce Operations Manager review and approval gate
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W1548_Assoc14" sourceRef="W1548_Annotation13" targetRef="W1548_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1548_Flow15" sourceRef="W1548_Start6" targetRef="W1548_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1548_Flow16" sourceRef="W1548_Task7" targetRef="W1548_Task8" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W1548_Flow17" sourceRef="W1548_Task8" targetRef="W1548_Task9" />
