    <bpmn:process id="W_W5500" name="W5500. Customer Digital Accessibility Program — WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance for Web, App &amp; Digital Channels" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: (a) Program establishment; (b) each ecommerce/app feature release (accessibility gate); (c) annual third-party audit; (d) new digital surface launch (app features per VS-75, kiosks per W924, self-checkout per VS-149)
Frequency: Release-gate checks continuous (~2–4 releases/month per the W828 cadence); automated scans weekly; assistive-user journey reviews quarterly; full third-party audit annual
Volume: ~35,000 active-SKU product pages + ~150 core journey pages (home, category/PDP, search, cart/checkout, account, service booking W923, order tracking, B2B punchout W1242) + app screens (VS-75) + kiosk/self-checkout UIs (W924/VS-149); benefiting customers include the statutory senior-citizen and PWD discount segments served at scale (VS-85) and situational/assistive users
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager
Participants: UX/UI Designer, Web/App Developers, QA (VS-27.1 W132 SDLC), Content/PIM team (VS-137/W50), Customer Service (VS-13), Legal &amp; Compliance, third-party accessibility auditor, Marketing
Source: workflow W5500 — Customer Digital Accessibility Program — WCAG 2.1 AA Compliance for Web, App &amp; Digital Channels</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5500_LaneSet5">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5500_Lane1" name="Ecommerce Ops Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Start6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5500_Lane2" name="QA">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5500_Lane3" name="Content Team">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5500_Lane4" name="CX Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5500_End15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5500_Start6" name="(a) Program establishment; (b) each ecommerce/app feature release (accessibility gate)…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow18</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task7" name="Adopt the standard &amp; publish the statement: WCAG 2.1 Level AA as the digital…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Adopt the standard &amp; publish the statement: WCAG 2.1 Level AA as the digital accessibility standard across web, app (VS-75), kiosk (W924), and self-checkout (VS-149); publish an accessibility statement with conformance status, feedback channel, and escalation path; align messaging with the store accessibility program (VS-07.2)
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Manager / Legal
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 3–5 days (initial)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow18</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task8" name="Baseline audit: automated scanning (axe-core in CI) plus manual audit with…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Baseline audit: automated scanning (axe-core in CI) plus manual audit with screen readers (NVDA/TalkBack/VoiceOver), keyboard-only navigation, contrast, zoom/reflow, and form/error labeling across the ~150 core journeys; sample-based PDP audit across categories; commission the annual third-party audit
Responsible (R): QA / UX / External Auditor
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 15–20 days (baseline); 5–8 days/year (re-audit)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task9" name="Remediation backlog: log all violations in the ecommerce board with severity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Remediation backlog: log all violations in the ecommerce board with severity (critical = blocks task completion); prioritize top revenue and statutory journeys first — checkout/payment, senior/PWD discount flows (VS-85), service booking (W923), order tracking, returns initiation (VS-32); fix SLAs by severity
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Manager / Developers
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task10" name="Release gate: add the accessibility checklist to the W828 definition-of-done…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Release gate: add the accessibility checklist to the W828 definition-of-done; component library tokens (contrast, focus states, touch targets) accessible by default; block release on critical violations; log exceptions with remediation dates
Responsible (R): QA / Developers
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: 1–2 hrs/release</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task11" name="Catalog content operations: mandatory alt-text field in PIM/DAM for hero and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Catalog content operations: mandatory alt-text field in PIM/DAM for hero and category images (VS-137/W50); accessible email/SMS templates (semantic HTML, link text); captions/transcripts for demo and how-to videos (W1239 content); merchandising rules for color-independent badging
Responsible (R): Content Team / PIM Owner
Accountable (A): Ecommerce Operations Manager
Duration: Continuous (part of W726 cadence)</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task12" name="Third-party surface governance: marketplace listings (VS-65) and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Third-party surface governance: marketplace listings (VS-65) and social-commerce content (W948/W1463) follow platform-accessible patterns; embedded widgets (payments, chat, maps) contractually required to meet WCAG 2.1 AA; vendor conformance evidence at onboarding and renewal
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Manager / Procurement
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 2–3 days/year + per vendor</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task13" name="Assistive customer support: contact-center agents trained on accessibility…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Assistive customer support: contact-center agents trained on accessibility requests and alternative order paths (phone-assisted order as documented fallback) (VS-13); accessibility-tagged tickets with response SLA; RA 7277 complaint escalation path to Legal (VS-100) if unresolved
Responsible (R): CX Lead / Legal
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: Training 0.5 day/year; continuous handling</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5500_Task14" name="Feedback loop &amp; monitoring: public feedback channel monitored weekly; quarterly…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Feedback loop &amp; monitoring: public feedback channel monitored weekly; quarterly conformance score by journey; assistive-technology usage analytics; KRIs (critical-violation count, feedback volume, complaint aging) reviewed in the ecommerce quarterly business review; social-metric contribution to VS-25.2 reporting where frameworks ask for it
Responsible (R): Ecommerce Ops Manager / Analytics
Accountable (A): GM, Digital Commerce Inc.
Duration: 1–2 days/quarter</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5500_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5500_End15" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5500_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5500_Annotation16">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-269 (ensure controlled execution — Ecommerce Platform Operations (PA-10.1).)
Owner: Ecommerce Operations Manager</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5500_Assoc17" sourceRef="W5500_Annotation16" targetRef="W5500_Start6" associationDirection="None" />
